de to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That's a one-line change plus the import.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** [#101](https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). My first attempt to open it timed out. I checked that no PR had been created, then retried with the same idempotency key. There's exactly one PR (#101).\n\nThe advisory tool doesn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't check the requirement itself. I relied on the test and the code comment, which both call for banker's rounding.\n\nI haven't merged it, because merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GwgmizYPiXqQnqaJ8xFsJL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_011oDjyZQWW45WXzutwt6NnK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py"}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01M2gN6Ti8KzY7xKDFnCZRe1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"id": "FIN-212"}, "name": "get_advisory", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_0145BvbeZCoWWVTwDsX9A6L6", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01UR96FjjZ9adKUPQwRdQmte", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "open"}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_013NDBuyfLFuGGF6tzaGK7FG", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money, per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01PVDcu8iX5P4deggtUMMxxZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01LVPQadEqttUiMBRJa7f9My", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01YBguZpG7zfWfBHMs3MYEkJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "`src/money.py` documented banker's rounding (FIN-212) but used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, causing `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build (e.g. 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66).\n\nThis switches the quantize rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_013S2z8ypcC6fZFj83C291UD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "all"}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Tn2YPVuLt29koqCrJYAkTo", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-half-even-rounding", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "`src/money.py` documented banker's rounding (FIN-212) but used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, causing `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build (e.g. 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66).\n\nThis switches the quantize rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-half-even-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Lftnf78F7pR8x9r1RBJS1c", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"state": "all"}, "name": "list_prs", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and the pull request is open against main with alex as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** In `src/money.py`, the comment for `round_money` says it uses banker's rounding (FIN-212), but the code used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. So 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of the 2.66 the test expects.\n- **Fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-half-even-rounding`, I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That's a one-line change plus the import.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.\n- **PR:** [#101](https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101). My first attempt to open it timed out. I checked that no PR had been created, then retried with the same idempotency key. There's exactly one PR (#101).\n\nThe advisory tool doesn't recognise FIN-212, so I couldn't check the requirement itself. I relied on the test and the code comment, which both call for banker's rounding.\n\nI haven't merged it, because merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}